WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.733 --> 00:00:16.719
Zann felt hope surge through him, along with new energy.

2
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.081
He ripped the bandage from his arm.

3
00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:24.364
Zira's purple goo had made the scrape feel better, but the injury was still visible.

4
00:00:25.304 --> 00:00:28.826
With one snap of his fingers, Zann healed it completely.

5
00:00:28.846 --> 00:00:30.327
"It's true!"

6
00:00:30.707 --> 00:00:32.048
he cried, dancing around.

7
00:00:32.816 --> 00:00:34.497
"Our magic is back!"

8
00:00:35.238 --> 00:00:39.140
Zing whistled and flew around in a circle, shooting blasts of flame.

9
00:00:40.001 --> 00:00:42.583
Perda laughed and started dancing along with Zann.

10
00:00:43.203 --> 00:00:49.107
They jumped and spun as the geyser of magic energy poured out of the well, drifting across the

11
00:00:49.147 --> 00:00:52.769
land. Suddenly Perda stopped and pointed.

12
00:00:52.789 --> 00:01:00.254
"Look!" Zann's gaze had been focused on Perda, who looked prettier than ever as she laughed and danced.

13
00:01:01.155 --> 00:01:02.476
Now he glanced around.

14
00:01:03.456 --> 00:01:06.877
The drab landscape surrounding them was changing.

15
00:01:07.718 --> 00:01:12.600
Bright green grass sprouted rapidly, replacing the dry brownish stuff.

16
00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.181
Flowers began to bloom.

17
00:01:15.721 --> 00:01:19.183
Moss crept out to cover the boulders with soft green.

18
00:01:20.343 --> 00:01:23.704
Even the scrawny little tree looked stronger and taller.

19
00:01:23.724 --> 00:01:25.945
"Careful, Zing!"

20
00:01:26.366 --> 00:01:32.028
Zann exclaimed as the little dragon zipped past the tree, almost setting it alight with his fiery breath.

21
00:01:32.824 --> 00:01:34.085
But the tree didn't burn.

22
00:01:34.925 --> 00:01:41.368
Zann wondered if that was because the air felt different now—moist and pleasant, with none of the baking

23
00:01:41.448 --> 00:01:42.948
heat of moments before.

24
00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:46.070
"This is amazing," Perda said.

25
00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:49.151
"It must have something to do with that root.

26
00:01:49.931 --> 00:01:54.033
The magic started pouring out as soon as Mellis chopped through it."

27
00:01:54.053 --> 00:01:56.854
"That makes sense," Zann agreed.

28
00:01:56.874 --> 00:02:00.556
"Oh! Speaking of Mellis, I hope this isn't freaking her out too much."

29
00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:04.010
Perda looked into the hole and gasped.

30
00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.451
"Mellis! Are you okay?"

31
00:02:07.272 --> 00:02:08.233
Zann hurried over.

32
00:02:09.073 --> 00:02:11.255
Mellis was huddled at the bottom of the hole.

33
00:02:12.076 --> 00:02:16.699
At first Zann thought she was watching the magic energy pour out from the severed root.

34
00:02:17.479 --> 00:02:19.901
Then he saw that her eyes were closed.

35
00:02:20.902 --> 00:02:22.003
"Oh no," he said.

36
00:02:22.023 --> 00:02:24.705
"All that magic energy must have knocked her out!"

37
00:02:25.605 --> 00:02:27.207
"We have to get her out of there."

38
00:02:27.867 --> 00:02:28.948
Perda held out her hand.

39
00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:35.723
"Grab my arm and lower me down there, and maybe we can—" "Wait—we have magic again," Zann reminded

40
00:02:35.763 --> 00:02:38.065
her. "Let's try to levitate her out."

41
00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.166
Perda's eyes widened.

42
00:02:41.146 --> 00:02:41.967
"You're right!"

43
00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:44.148
she exclaimed with a sheepish laugh.

44
00:02:44.168 --> 00:02:46.049
"I almost forgot."

45
00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:50.151
They created friction and focused on lifting Mellis.

46
00:02:50.171 --> 00:02:53.373
"Levitate," Zann murmured.

47
00:02:54.414 --> 00:02:58.196
Slowly and carefully they brought Mellis up and out of the hole.

48
00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:04.336
Zing flew around, whistling anxiously until Mellis landed gently on the ground.

49
00:03:04.356 --> 00:03:08.158
"Mellis!" Perda leaned over her.

50
00:03:08.178 --> 00:03:09.499
"Can you hear me?"

51
00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:13.502
Mellis' hand twitched, and her eyes fluttered open.

52
00:03:13.522 --> 00:03:16.023
"Wh-what happened?"

53
00:03:16.484 --> 00:03:16.964
she asked.

54
00:03:16.984 --> 00:03:20.566
"You released a bunch of magic energy," Zann said.

55
00:03:20.586 --> 00:03:21.787
"Look around and see!"

56
00:03:22.928 --> 00:03:23.708
Mellis sat up.

57
00:03:24.529 --> 00:03:27.011
She gasped as she took in the scene around her.

58
00:03:27.031 --> 00:03:28.552
"Where are we?"

59
00:03:29.324 --> 00:03:30.525
Her voice was shaking.

60
00:03:32.066 --> 00:03:32.867
Perda smiled.

61
00:03:32.887 --> 00:03:35.468
"We're in the same place," she said.

62
00:03:35.488 --> 00:03:38.170
"I guess the energy made stuff grow.

63
00:03:38.911 --> 00:03:40.892
And Zann and I can do magic again.

64
00:03:41.272 --> 00:03:46.856
Watch!" She snapped her fingers and created a glass of water, which she handed to Mellis.

65
00:03:47.817 --> 00:03:50.519
Mellis stared at it, seeming afraid to drink it.

66
00:03:51.379 --> 00:03:53.621
Zann was still thinking about what had happened.

67
00:03:54.321 --> 00:03:56.383
"That root contained magic," he said.

68
00:03:56.403 --> 00:03:57.724
"But how?"

69
00:03:58.924 --> 00:04:03.447
"Different worlds get their magic energy in different ways," Perda reminded him.

70
00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:05.809
"Like in Atmo—remember?

71
00:04:06.509 --> 00:04:09.751
There, magic energy is created by the air itself.

72
00:04:10.692 --> 00:04:16.816
But in Magica it comes out into the air through the tree, or maybe from the vortex itself

73
00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:17.637
through the tree.

74
00:04:18.877 --> 00:04:20.398
Other worlds are all different.

75
00:04:21.379 --> 00:04:27.083
Some have weak energy, like Wyssa's home world—" "Or Terrica, before now," Zann added.

76
00:04:27.883 --> 00:04:28.584
Perda nodded.

77
00:04:29.224 --> 00:04:33.247
"Then there are worlds with extra strong magic, like Galvan.

78
00:04:33.867 --> 00:04:36.329
Remember how weird it felt to do magic there?"

79
00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:38.771
Mellis looked overwhelmed.

80
00:04:38.791 --> 00:04:41.913
"But how could things change so suddenly?"

81
00:04:42.774 --> 00:04:44.895
She carefully set down the glass of water.

82
00:04:44.915 --> 00:04:47.917
"It's like we're not even in Terrica anymore!"

83
00:04:47.937 --> 00:04:50.939
"Oh, we are," Zann assured her.

84
00:04:50.959 --> 00:04:52.861
"But now we can do magic."

85
00:04:52.881 --> 00:04:55.602
"Maybe you can too," Perda said.

86
00:04:55.622 --> 00:04:57.544
"Give it a try—let's see!"

87
00:04:58.264 --> 00:04:59.485
Mellis looked nervous.

88
00:04:59.505 --> 00:05:01.627
"Me, do magic?

89
00:05:02.488 --> 00:05:03.529
But I don't know how!"

90
00:05:03.549 --> 00:05:06.912
"It's not that hard," Zann said.

91
00:05:06.932 --> 00:05:09.454
"Even really young kids can do basic stuff."

92
00:05:10.035 --> 00:05:12.196
He frowned as Zing zipped past.

93
00:05:12.937 --> 00:05:16.520
The little dragon was obviously happy to have his fire power back.

94
00:05:17.421 --> 00:05:20.704
He shot out a burst of flames that knocked over the water glass.

95
00:05:20.724 --> 00:05:25.128
"Hey, stop that, you overgrown swamp rat," Zann scolded him.

96
00:05:25.888 --> 00:05:29.230
Perda smiled encouragingly at Mellis, ignoring Zing.

97
00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.331
"Just create friction.

98
00:05:32.071 --> 00:05:33.852
Rub your hands together like this."

99
00:05:34.573 --> 00:05:35.333
She demonstrated.

100
00:05:35.353 --> 00:05:40.156
"While you do that, picture what you want to create in your mind.

101
00:05:40.836 --> 00:05:43.698
It can be anything—maybe another glass of water?"

102
00:05:44.939 --> 00:05:46.399
Mellis looked uncertain.

103
00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:52.383
But she rubbed her hands together and then squeezed her eyes shut, looking very focused.

104
00:05:53.103 --> 00:06:00.512
For a moment nothing happened, and Zann wondered if Terricans were like Voids—unable to do magic at all.

105
00:06:01.272 --> 00:06:08.277
He shouted in surprise as rain abruptly began pelting down, as if a giant waterfall had just burst

106
00:06:08.317 --> 00:06:09.658
into existence overhead.

107
00:06:10.338 --> 00:06:12.920
He quickly snapped his fingers to create an umbrella.

108
00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:14.641
Perda did the same.

109
00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:21.125
Zing flew down to huddle beneath Zann's umbrella, chirping irritably about getting wet.

110
00:06:22.226 --> 00:06:24.588
Perda moved over to cover Mellis with her umbrella.

111
00:06:25.436 --> 00:06:28.298
"I think you just created rain," Perda said.

112
00:06:28.318 --> 00:06:30.620
"I can't believe I did this."

113
00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:35.503
Mellis was staring, wide-eyed, at the puddles forming all around them.

114
00:06:35.523 --> 00:06:38.065
"And why is the rain pink?"

115
00:06:38.926 --> 00:06:39.706
Zann shrugged.

116
00:06:39.726 --> 00:06:43.889
"Pink rain isn't as common as green or purple, but it's not that rare, either."

117
00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.451
"Not in Magica," Perda said.

118
00:06:46.471 --> 00:06:48.292
"Things might be different here."

119
00:06:48.312 --> 00:06:51.694
"Green? Purple?"

120
00:06:52.475 --> 00:06:53.616
Mellis looked baffled.

121
00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:56.382
"Rain isn't usually a color at all!

122
00:06:57.023 --> 00:06:59.145
It's just clear, like regular water."

123
00:06:59.165 --> 00:07:02.248
"Hmm." Perda looked thoughtful.

124
00:07:02.768 --> 00:07:05.291
"We've seen other worlds with colorless rain."

125
00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:10.476
Zann knew she was right, though he couldn't remember exactly which worlds.

126
00:07:10.496 --> 00:07:17.622
"Mellis!" he exclaimed in alarm as Mellis' eyes fluttered shut again and she keeled over with a splash.
